cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Counterproof in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Counterproof: verifying that code changes by AI coding agents are proven by their tests"
abstract: >-
  Counterproof is a local-first command-line tool that decides whether a code change written
  by an AI coding agent is actually proven by its tests, not just green. It runs five probes
  against the change in isolated git worktrees (a claim audit of the agent's session,
  test-integrity checks, red-green, change-scoped mutation testing and a blind test oracle)
  and maps the evidence to one of five verdicts with deterministic rules; no language model
  decides the verdict.
